    <li>Dennis, Richard, &ldquo;<a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="http://www.frbsf.org/economic-research/publications/economic-letter/2005/november/uncertainty-and-monetary-policy-2005/" class="offsite" target="_blank">Uncertainty and Monetary Policy</a>,&rdquo;&nbsp;<em>Economic Letter</em>, Federal Reserve Bank of San Francisco, Number 2005-33, November 30, 2005.</li>
    <li>Giannoni, Marc P., &ldquo;Does Model Uncertainty Justify Caution? Robust Optimal Monetary Policy in a Forward-Looking Model,&rdquo;&nbsp;<em>Macroeconomic Dynamics</em>&nbsp;6, 2002, pp. 111-141.</li>
    <li>Giannoni, Marc P., &ldquo;Robust Optimal Monetary Policy in a Forward-Looking Model with Parameter and Shock Uncertainty,&rdquo;&nbsp;<em>Journal of Applied Econometrics</em>&nbsp;22, 2007, pp. 179-213.</li>
    <li>Greenspan, Alan, &ldquo;<a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="http://www.federalreserve.gov/boarddocs/speeches/2004/20040103/default.htm" class="offsite" target="_blank">Risk and Uncertainty in Monetary Policy</a>,&rdquo; remarks at the Meetings of the American Economic Association, San Diego, CA, January 3, 2004 (and published in the&nbsp;<em>American Economic Review: Papers and Proceedings</em>&nbsp;94, May 2004, pp. 33-40).</li>
    <li>Hansen, Lars Peter, and Thomas J. Sargent, &ldquo;Wanting Robustness in Macroeconomics,&rdquo; Chapter 20 in Benjamin J. Friedman and Michael Woodford, eds.,&nbsp;<em>Handbook of Monetary Economics</em>&nbsp;3B, Amsterdam, Netherlands: Elsevier-North-Holland, 2011, pp. 1097-1157.</li>
    <li>Hansen, Lars Peter, and Thomas J. Sargent,&nbsp;<em>Robustness</em>, Princeton, NJ: Princeton University Press, 2007.</li>
    <li>Hansen, Lars Peter, and Thomas J. Sargent, &ldquo;<a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="http://www.imes.boj.or.jp/english/publication/mes/2001/me19-s1-9.pdf" class="offsite" target="_blank">Acknowledging Misspecification in Macroeconomic Theory</a>,&rdquo;&nbsp;<em>Monetary and Economic Studies (Special Edition)</em>, Bank of Japan&rsquo;s Institute for Monetary and Economic Studies, February 2001, pp. 213-225.</li>
    <li>Hetzel, Robert L., &ldquo;<a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.richmondfed.org/-/media/richmondfedorg/publications/research/working_papers/2016/pdf/wp16-11.pdf" class="offsite" target="_blank">A Proposal to Clarify the Objectives and Strategy of Monetary Policy</a>,&rdquo; Federal Reserve Bank of Richmond Working Paper No. 16-11, September 12, 2016.</li>
    <li>Manski, Charles F., &ldquo;Policy Analysis with Incredible Certitude,&rdquo;&nbsp;<em>The Economic Journal</em>&nbsp;121, August 2011, pp. F261-F288.</li>
    <li>Manski, Charles F., &ldquo;Communicating Uncertainty in Official Economic Statistics: An Appraisal Fifty Years after Morgenstern,&rdquo;&nbsp;<em>Journal of Economic Literature</em>&nbsp;53, 2015, pp. 631-653.</li>
    <li>Mester, Loretta J., &ldquo;<a href="/collections/speeches/2014/sp-20141120-forward-guidance-and-communications">Forward Guidance and Communications in U.S. Monetary Policy</a>,&rdquo; remarks at the Imperial Business Insights Series, Imperial College, London, UK, November 20, 2014.</li>
    <li>Mester, Loretta J., &ldquo;<a href="/collections/speeches/2016/sp-20160401-the-outlook-for-the-economy-and-monetary-policy">The Outlook for the Economy and Monetary Policy: Low-Frequency Policymaking in a High-Frequency World</a>,&rdquo; remarks at the New York Association for Business Economics, New York, NY, April 1, 2016.</li>
    <li>Morgenstern, Oskar,&nbsp;<em>On the Accuracy of Economic Observations</em>, Princeton, NJ: Princeton University Press, 1950; second edition, 1963.</li>
    <li>Orphanides, Athanasios, &ldquo;Inflation Dynamics: Lessons From Past Debates for Current Policy,&rdquo; remarks at the Federal Reserve Bank of Kansas City Economic Policy Symposium, Jackson Hole, WY, August 29, 2015.</li>
