    <li>Orphanides, Athanasios, and John C. Williams, &ldquo;Robust Monetary Policy with Imperfect Knowledge,&rdquo;&nbsp;<em>Journal of Monetary Economics</em>&nbsp;54, 2007, pp. 1406-1435.</li>
    <li>Orphanides, Athanasios, and John C. Williams, &ldquo;Robust Monetary Policy Rules with Unknown Natural Rates,&rdquo;&nbsp;<em>Brookings Papers on Economic Activity</em>&nbsp;2, 2002, pp. 63-145.</li>
    <li>Sargent, Thomas J., &ldquo;Discussion of &lsquo;Policy Rules for Open Economies,&rsquo;by Laurence Ball,&rdquo; remarks at the NBER Conference on Monetary Policy Rules, Islamorada, FL, January 15-17, 1998.</li>
    <li>Taylor, John B. &ldquo;<a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.ciaonet.org/attachments/23607/uploads" class="offsite" target="_blank">Monetary Policy During the Past 30 Years with Lessons for the Next 30 Years</a>,&rdquo; luncheon address at the Cato Institute&rsquo;s 30th Annual Monetary Conference on Money, Markets and Government: The Next 30 Years, Washington, D.C., November 15, 2012 (published in&nbsp;<em>Cato Journal</em>&nbsp;33, Fall 2013, pp. 333-334).</li>
    <li>Waggoner, Daniel F., and Tao Zha, &ldquo;Confronting Model Misspecification in Macroeconomics,&rdquo;&nbsp;<em>Journal of Econometrics</em>&nbsp;171, 2012, pp. 167-184.</li>
    <li>Wieland, Volker, Tobias Cwik, Gernot J. M&uuml;ller, Sebastian Schmidt, and Maik Wolters, &ldquo;<a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0167268112000157" class="offsite" target="_blank">A New Comparative Approach to Macroeconomic Modeling and Policy Analysis</a>,&rdquo;&nbsp;<em>Journal of Economic Behavior and Organization</em>&nbsp;83, 2012, pp. 523-541.</li>
    <li>Woodford, Michael, &ldquo;<a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.kansascityfed.org/publicat/sympos/2012/Woodford_final.pdf" class="offsite" target="_blank">Methods of Policy Accommodation at the Interest-Rate Lower Bound</a>,&rdquo; in&nbsp;<em>The Changing Policy Landscape</em>, Federal Reserve Bank of Kansas City Economic Symposium, Jackson Hole, WY, 2012, pp. 185-288.</li>
    <li>Yellen, Janet L., &ldquo;<a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="http://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/speech/yellen20160826a.htm" class="offsite" target="_blank">The Federal Reserve&rsquo;s Monetary Policy Toolkit: Past, Present, and Future</a>,&rdquo; remarks at &ldquo;Designing Resilient Monetary Policy Frameworks for the Future,&rdquo; a symposium sponsored by the Federal Reserve Bank of Kansas City, Jackson Hole, WY, August 26, 2016.</li>
</ul>        </div>
    </div>
